00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.680
I love you, too!

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:13.350
I guess you were
actually cute once, too, Koi.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.980
I guess that might've happened.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.810
I do remember not being satisfied and
tying one fly after another though.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:24.650
When I told Koharu about that,
she said she wanted to try out fly tying.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.030
"Tying"?

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.570
Oh, that's what it's called
when you make your own flies.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:32.120
Teach me everything you know, Miss Koi!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.040
Sure, I guess.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.000
So, what did you want to make?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.630
There's actually a fly
that I want to replace.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.460
This one!

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.800
Ah, an Elk Hair Caddis.
It's pretty beat up.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.430
An Elk... what now?

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.010
An Elk Hair Caddis.
They work really great.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.350
Yeah, exactly!

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:56.730
And you can still see it
really well after you cast it!

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:00.560
All right, let's get started.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.230
First, you need your vise.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:05.650
A bobbin holder, a hackle plier,

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:09.780
a bodkin with a half hitch, and scissors.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:13.370
I think that's pretty much
all you need for fly tying.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.870
This many?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:19.540
Oh, and a hair stacker. You'll definitely
need that for an Elk Hair Caddis.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.250
"Vise" "Scissors" "Bodkin with a Half Hitch"
"Bobbin" "Hackle Plier" "Hair Stacker"

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.250
So many foreign words at once...

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.090
"Vise" "Scissors" "Bodkin with a Half Hitch"
"Bobbin" "Hackle Plier" "Hair Stacker"

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.090
You don't have to try
to remember them all at once.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:25.510
You don't have to try
to remember them all at once.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.470
Maybe we should use a #12 for the hook...

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:31.510
The numbers for the sizes of
the hooks are the opposite of rods,

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:35.810
and the they go up as the
hooks get smaller, so be careful.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.940
First, set your hook into the vise.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.190
The first thing you'll
be using a thin thread.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:46.820
You're going to wrap
this around the hook like so.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.950
Next, you'll be using some cock hackles.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.700
They're rooster feathers.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.530
Huh... so like chicken feathers.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:59.330
Take one, and you want
to fray out the feather.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.500
Then you'll cut off a little from the tip.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:07.170
Flip the reverse side up
and attach it to the hook.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:11.380
Then you'll attach the
hackle plier on the other end

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.100
and set it somewhere
it won't get in the way.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:18.600
Next, you'll need some dubbing material.
We'll be using wool this time.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.980
Wool... Oh, sheep.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.900
Once you apply some wax on the thread,

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.740
apply the dubbing
material from top to bottom.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.660
Keep applying the dubbing
material just before the hole.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:38.080
Then you'll grab the plier and
wrap the hackle around equally.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.580
Ooh! It's looking more
and more like a fly!

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.460
Once you're done wrapping,
set hackle in place with the thread,

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:48.420
and cut off any of the excess.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.090
And finally, we'll be using the elk hair.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.760
Ah, so it's a deer this time.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:01.430
Put the elk hair you cut
into the hair stacker.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.350
Wha--?!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:07.270
Many a fly fishermen would get yelled
at by their families for this noise.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.440
That's hilarious!

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.820
Is it?

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:15.740
Once you take out the elk hair
from the end of the stacker,

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:19.240
figure out how much you want sticking out,
and then tie it down with the thread.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.410
Gradually increase the
strength that you're wrapping it in,

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.290
and once you've wrapped it
about ten times, pick up the head,

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.750
and wrap it onto
the hook about five times.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.760
Then when you wrapped it five
more times using the half hitch,

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.300
use the tip of the bodkin to apply some
head cement where you tied the thread.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.300
"Head Cement (Glue)" "Bodkin"

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.300
use the tip of the bodkin to apply some
head cement where you tied the thread.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.720
"Head Cement (Glue)" "Bodkin"

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.720
It smells weird...

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:37.850
It smells weird...

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:43.730
Cut off the thread and once you cut
the elk-hair head the way you want...

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:47.270
Your Elk Hair Caddis is complete.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:50.320
That's amazing! It looks just
like the ones in the store!

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.240
I mean, I do sell them.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.450
Well? You think you got it?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.280
Yeah! I'll give it a try!

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.260
"Tap Tap Tap Tap Tap Tap Tap Tap Tap Tap"

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.850
I... I did it!

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:26.640
The first fly I tied all by myself!

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:31.110
Chickens, sheep, and deer...

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.690
So the art of tying...

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:37.110
...ts actually the forbidden art
of creating a chimera!

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.120
Yeah, it's really not.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.660
You can have the ones I made, Koharu.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.500
Whoa! You already made this many?!

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.290
They're so nice...

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:55.470
I don't usually make these,
so I can't get them as nice as Koi's.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.510
Really?

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.260
I catch so many with them
that I don't use them often.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.010
You miser!

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.720
Don't worry.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:06.180
It looks like you'll be able to catch
some with the ones you two made.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.980
Huh? But...

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.900
It's not as nice as yours, Koi.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:15.110
Any fly counts as long
as it can catch some fish.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:17.400
Wow, that's deep.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.490
I can't wait to use this!

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.620
Oh, in that case...

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:30.500
Wow...

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.170
It's so pretty!

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.500
The leaves are definitely
autumn colors now.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.590
We haven't been here
since summer vacation!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.970
Girls! We're going to start soon!

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.010
Okay!

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:50.440
Everyone, I thank you all
for gathering here today.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:54.770
Our annual one-fly
tournament is about to begin!

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.940
Yeah!

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.490
--That scared me...
--I'm gonna win this year!

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:00.070
--Wow...
--I'll show you the results
from all my training!

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.870
It's a huge deal each year.

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:05.080
I'm getting fired up!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.700
The rules are simple.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.200
You can only use one fly.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:13.080
The person to catch the
biggest fish within an hour wins.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:18.840
As a special rule, any of the beginners
or kiddos can change their flies.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.430
We got some fabulous prizes
yet again this year!

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:25.140
Yeah!

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:27.310
Fifth place gets a waterproof backpack.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.850
Fourth place gets a fly rod.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:30.730
Third place gets a fly reel.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.850
So fancy...

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.400
Believe it or not, for second place...

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:39.530
You get an AI-powered
robot vacuum cleaner!

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.910
Any of you folks who upset your
family by coming here today

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.410
might want to go for that prize.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:47.910
And for first place...

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.500
...is a giant body pillow!

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.420
Whoa! Hiyori's all fired up!

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:01.680
All right. Let's let the fishing begin!

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.930
Yeah!

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:08.930
