00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:28.720
What? But you're not supposed
to change your fly, are you?

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:31.930
You're a beginner, so you can change it.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.020
I feel like I've lost!

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:40.440
What exactly are you fighting with?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.440
I'm pretty sure I told you that
you change up the fly you use

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.490
depending on the place and season.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.610
Yeah.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:50.830
Even though you're fishing for the same
fish in the same spot you did before,

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:54.200
you're getting
completely different results.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.080
The weather that day or
the conditions of the river...

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:01.210
The types of bugs that may
or may not be in the river...

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.090
You can't just think about the fish.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:08.090
Thinking about their environment
and going through trial and error

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.640
might be fun, too.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:17.350
Their environment... huh.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.770
You brought your fly box
that Hiyori gave you, right?

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.190
Huh? Yeah.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.650
I'll choose which one
would be best for you.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:31.200
But I wanna catch one
with the fly that I tied myself!

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:34.160
I mean, I get you, but...

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.330
I wonder what kind of fly Hiyori's using.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:42.590
Hiyori's using a <i>marabou </i>fly.

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:44.710
She's pretty serious.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.760
She keeps pulling on it little by little.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.930
She's retrieving her line.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:54.810
She's making it look like
a little fish to entice the fish.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:56.930
It's just like using a lure.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.150
She got a bite!

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.480
Oh, no... It's getting away.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.530
It's definitely running.

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:09.070
Running?

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:12.990
If she pulls too hard, the line might
break, or the fish might catch on,

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.410
so she's feeding the line to go
along with the fish's movements.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:21.330
And once the fish gets tired
and can't swim as fast anymore...

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.880
You go for it.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.500
She's using a reel!

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.880
Looks like a big one.
I'm gonna go help her out.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.680
O-Okay.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:33.600
Hiyori.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.930
Okay.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:55.870
It's about 36 centimeters.
It's nice and fat.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.950
What a pretty rainbow.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.830
Great job, Hiyori.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.920
Thanks, Koi.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:08.250
Mrrr...

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:10.840
Whatever. I'll catch one, too.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.090
But I won't be able to at this rate...

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.800
I know!

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:19.020
If I just sink it like I did
the time I caught a char...

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:23.020
And I'll cast it right in front
of the fish at the bottom...

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:25.310
Then pull in little by little...

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.320
It's chasing it!

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:30.400
It ate it!

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:33.660
I couldn't tell with the char
since I caught it coincidentally,

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:36.410
but I wonder if it
chased after my line, too.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.250
I did it!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:46.790
It's not as big as Hiyori's, but
I caught it with the fly I tied myself!

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:50.380
Okay, time for a picture... Huh?

00:16:55.760 --> 00:17:01.810
No! No... No... No...

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.020
Koharu...

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.190
Happy Birthday!

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.860
Aw, thank you...

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.980
This is from my sister.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:15.320
Wow! The food's ready, so come on up.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:18.120
Hey, Futaba and Aiko. Welcome.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.370
Heya.

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:20.490
Hello.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:23.500
Oh, are we having hot pot today?

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.080
Wrong!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.420
The correct answer is...

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:31.840
Rainbow trout <i>takikomi gohan</i>!

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:37.970
This is the rainbow trout that
got you first place, right, Hiyori?

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:40.850
Yup. I caught that one.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:41.970
Heh.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:45.270
And I cooked it!

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.560
That's so cool!

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:52.480
Be careful of any small bones.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.780
I will.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.360
Let's eat!

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.210
It's so good!

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.290
The rainbow trout is so fluffy.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.170
The flower-shaped carrots are so cute.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:13.420
"Heh"

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:13.420
The flower-shaped carrots are so cute.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.380
"Heh"

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.380
Oh, you bet they are.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:15.590
Oh, you bet they are.

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:18.050
The rice has a hint of sweetness, too.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.550
Yes.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:24.220
I already ate it all...

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:26.230
There's plenty more where that came from.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:28.310
I'll get you more!

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:33.730
Since you got first place, Hiyori,
I'll give you some of the charred bits.

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:36.950
Koharu, I'd like some more, too, please.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:40.280
M-Me, too...

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.200
Eat up, all of you.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:45.540
Please teach me some cooking
next time we catch some fish.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.960
Me, too.

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.370
Yeah, sure!

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.210
We can use whatever fish
you want to catch next time, Futaba.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.130
We're already talking about next time?

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:55.170
This is the problem with you fishing nuts.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.550
Oh, please. You know
you're coming with us, Koi.

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:00.760
F-Futaba, I'll go, too.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:03.350
Sure, I'll teach you how to fish.

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.100
K-Koharu--

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:11.310
Koharu!

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:15.070
Here's our gift to you.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.860
We made it together!

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:20.160
Wow, how cute!

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.660
You bundled up a bunch of hair
accessories. Thank you so much!

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:25.330
Koharu.

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.160
This is from me.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.330
Yay! Thank you, Koi!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.210
Oooh, what is it? Can I open it?

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:32.540
Of course.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.210
Ooh, an apron!

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:38.670
It's made out of cotton material,
so it's resistant against sparks,

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:40.380
and there are plenty of pockets,

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:44.180
so it'll probably be ideal for
cooking on our camping trips.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:49.020
Thank you! It's cute,
so I'll use it at home, too!

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.980
I'm so happy.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.730
Oh, you bought a new phone?

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:57.570
Yeah.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:02.070
Considering how much it'd cost to repair,
I figured I'd just get a new one.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:05.370
And repairing it won't
bring my photos back.

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:10.250
Goodbye, my memories.

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:12.920
You sure it didn't automatically
get saved to some cloud?

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.080
Huh?

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.840
They're here!

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:21.550
My pictures from summer vacation...
From the cultural fair...

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:24.890
All of the photos
from our camping trips...

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.720
Thank you so much, Koi!

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:31.940
That's great, Koharu.

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:33.730
Yeah!

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:43.360
I thought you were
born in the spring, Koharu.

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:45.870
Yeah. My name has
the word for spring in it,

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:47.870
so it's super confusing.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:51.080
"Koharu" is actually a word
associated with winter, isn't it?

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.960
Yup!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:55.460
Once autumn is about to end,

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.210
and it starts to get chillier,

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:03.380
the period of calm, autumn days
where you get a bit of warmth

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:04.970
like spring is called "Koharu."

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:06.850
Oh, so it's like today!

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.350
Yup!

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:11.520
Hiyori, come here a sec.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:13.440
Don't you want to give her your present?

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:18.270
I-I do... But mine's sorta plain,
so I'm not sure what to do.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:25.280
Whatever, but you should probably hurry up
or you might have some trouble later.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:28.740
Huh? What do you mean?

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:32.250
Thank you all for coming!

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:33.960
Thank you for having us over!

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.670
All right, see you later.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:36.830
Yup.

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:40.630
Okay, I guess we can start clea--

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:49.260
K-Koharu... Are you mad about something?

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:52.310
Nope. I'm not mad at all.

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:54.430
Yup. She's mad.

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:58.060
Why, though? Did I do
something to upset her?

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:58.860
"Gloom Gloom Gloom Gloom"

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:58.860
Why, though? Did I do
something to upset her?

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:02.780
"Gloom Gloom Gloom Gloom"

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:02.780
Now that I think about it,
it's her birthday, and she had to cook!

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.490
"Gloom Gloom Gloom Gloom"

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.490
I made her work way too much!

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:04.860
I made her work way too much!

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:09.160
I get it... I didn't do enough.

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:23.050
Hiyori, you gave Koi a birthday present,
but didn't get me anything...

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:26.760
But it's not like I'm mad
about that or anything!

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:28.300
Oh, jeez! You made me say it!

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:32.060
I'm not supposed to say stuff like that!

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:36.390
Actually, I have one for you...

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:41.360
A photo album?

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:45.110
It's not cute at all compared
to everyone else's gifts...

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:48.660
And we found out that
you didn't lose your pictures,

00:22:48.660 --> 00:22:51.160
so it was sort of
awkward to give it to you.

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:54.240
Hiyori... When you give
someone something like this,

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:56.960
you're supposed to include
some pictures and a message.

00:22:56.960 --> 00:22:58.960
Huh? Really?

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:06.590
But I figured that you might want
to pick out your own pictures.

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:16.930
Then let's pick some out together.

00:23:16.930 --> 00:23:18.600
Okay!

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:22.610
We're home!

00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:26.360
Koharu, we bought your cake!

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:29.070
Oh?

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:30.860
Koharu, what about this picture?

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:34.030
What? No way. I don't
look that cute in that one.

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:36.450
Let's print this one instead.

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:38.910
I can't tell the difference...

00:23:38.910 --> 00:23:41.080
You totally can!

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:43.590
How about this one?

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:47.840
Ooh, nice! Everyone looks
really nice in that one.

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:51.590
After looking at all of these pictures,
I want to go fishing!

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:53.010
Yeah.

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.970
Where should we go next?

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:57.720
Hm...

00:23:57.720 --> 00:23:59.060
I know!

00:23:59.060 --> 00:24:02.810
If it's nice out tomorrow,
let's go to the ocean!

00:24:02.810 --> 00:24:04.520
Yeah!

00:24:04.520 --> 00:24:04.810
"Congratulations on winning
the one-fly tournament, Hiyori!"

00:24:04.520 --> 00:24:04.810
Yeah!

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:08.610
"Congratulations on winning
the one-fly tournament, Hiyori!"

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:08.610
Hopefully, we'll catch a lot of fish!

00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:09.740
"Congratulations on winning
